## Why This Question Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to design per-key rate-limiting state, implement TTL-based eviction, ensure idempotence across replays, and align with KCNA consumer semantics.

## Key Concepts
- Per-key sliding or fixed-window counters
- TTL-based eviction and memory safety
- Idempotence with replay handling
- Backpressure and stable commit boundaries

## Code Example
```javascript
class RateStore {
  constructor(ttlMs) {
    this.ttlMs = ttlMs;
    this.store = new Map();
  }
  get(key, minute) {
    return this.store.get(`${key}:${minute}`) ?? 0;
  }
  increment(key, minute) {
    const entry = this.store.get(`${key}:${minute}`) ?? { count: 0, timestamp: Date.now() };
    entry.count++;
    this.store.set(`${key}:${minute}`, entry);
    return entry.count;
  }
  prune() {
    const now = Date.now();
    for (const [key, entry] of this.store.entries()) {
      if (now - entry.timestamp > this.ttlMs) {
        this.store.delete(key);
      }
    }
  }
}

class AlertingSink {
  constructor(limit = 100, windowMs = 60000) {
    this.rateStore = new RateStore(windowMs);
    this.limit = limit;
    this.seenMessages = new Set();
  }
  onMessage(ctx, msg) {
    if (this.seenMessages.has(msg.offset)) return;
    this.seenMessages.add(msg.offset);

    const minute = Math.floor(Date.now() / 60000);
    const count = this.rateStore.increment(msg.key, minute);
    if (count <= this.limit) {
      ctx.emitAlert(msg);
    }
  }
  commitOffsets() {}
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design non-intrusive monitoring in KCNA, track per-partition state, and emit reliable alerts without affecting throughput.

## Key Concepts
- Per-partition lag tracking
- End offsets vs committed offsets
- Non-intrusive monitoring
- Idempotent alerting and deduplication

## Code Example
```javascript
class LagMonitor {
  constructor(threshold, windowMs = 60000) {
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.windowMs = windowMs;
    this.lagMap = new Map();
    this.lastAlert = new Map();
  }
  onMessage(partition, endOffset, committedOffset) {
    const lag = endOffset - committedOffset;
    const now = Date.now();
    this.lagMap.set(partition, { lag, ts: now });
    this.check(partition);
  }
  check(partition) {
    const entry = this.lagMap.get(partition);
    if (!entry) return;
    if (entry.lag > this.threshold && (Date.now() - entry.ts) >= this.windowMs) {
      this.emitAlert(partition, entry.lag);
      this.lastAlert.set(partition, Date.now());
      // reset timer for next alert window
      this.lagMap.set(partition, { lag: entry.lag, ts: Date.now() });
    }
  }
  emitAlert(partition, lag) {
    // publish to 'lag_alerts' with partition, lag, timestamp, host
  }
}
```

